@startuml getUuidOfTheProtocol
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title
getUuidOfTheProtocol – Retrieve TCP Server UUID by Protocol
end title

participant "requestor" as requestor
participant "TCP Server Interface " as tsr #LightCyan
participant "JSON Driver" as jd #LightYellow
participant "config.json" as cfg #LightGrey

note over requestor
  - protocol 
end note

requestor -> tsr: (protocol)
activate tsr

tsr -> jd: read logical-termination-points
activate jd

jd <-> cfg: retrieve control-construct

jd --> tsr: TCP server LTP list
deactivate jd

note over tsr
  <u>Processing</u>
  - Iterate through TCP server LTPs  
  - Read tcp-server-interface-configuration  
  - Match local-protocol with input protocol  
  - Extract UUID of matching TCP server  
  - Return UUID if found  
  - Return undefined if no match exists
end note

tsr --> requestor: tcpServerUuid | undefined
deactivate tsr

@enduml
